JO  - Journal of Hohai University
DO  - 
AB  - Based on the MODIS/Terra snow cover datasets from 2000 to 2009,the spatial distribution and seasonal variation of snow cover over five rivers' source regions in the Tibetan Plateau were analyzed.The results show that in contrast to the north of the study areas,the most persistently snow-covered areas were concentrated in the Yarlung Zangbo Valley and the Nyainqentanglha and southern Hengduan mountains.In spring and winter,the mean snow cover fraction was at its maximum,with two peak values in February and November.Trend changes could be observed in the study areas in different seasons.There was a significant decreasing trend of snow cover in the source region of the Brahmaputra River in the spring and a significant increasing trend in the source region of the Yangtze River in the autumn.A slight decreasing trend of the snow cover was detected in the source regions of the Yellow River,the Lancang River,and the Salween River in the winter.The snow cover over the source regions of the Yangtze River and the Brahmaputra River was increasing,and the increasing trend was significant in the source region of the Yangtze River.In general,the snow cover over the five rivers' source regions showed a slight increasing trend.
