AB  - The spatial-temporal monitoring of regional snow covered area has important significance for the determination of regional snow disaster impact scope and disaster grade.The spatial and temporal changes pattern of snow cover in Xinjiang was analyzed by 10 years Aqua/MODIS snow products which were composed according to maximum area rule.The results indicated that snow cover fluctuated and had a decreasing trend,the permanent snow cover area was spatially distributed Altay mountains,northern parts of Tianshan and southwest part of Kulun mountians area,and the snow cover area changes were caused by the changes of snow cover in grassland area of basin between Tian shan mountains and Altay mountain area.
